{"item_id":"E-RES-607","ledger":[{"claim_id":"Q01","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The intended reader is an owner-operator of a 1–10 person small business."},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"a six-person D2C online shop whose owner compares an automation investment with the cost of another hire"},{"source_id":"C01","quote":"The representative pains are 8–10 hours a week of repeated customer questions, neglected sales leads,
  and manual invoice/data work."}],"rationale":"This is a planned instruction to define an abstract topic and anchor it to the approved persona context; it asserts no current Bareni capability, customer or observed result. "Neglected sales leads" and the D2C persona are approved framing material.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed as an illustrative definition. Present the D2C shop or service-business example as a persona scenario, not as an existing customer or observed case, and do not attach any figure (including 8–10 hours) as a measured outcome."},{"claim_id":"Q02","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"explain one observable workflow decision, threshold, diagnostic question,
  control, or next step"},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Numbers require a source and status."}],"rationale":"An instruction to pose a diagnostic question and name illustrative decay signals, with an explicit ban on invented metrics. It does not assert an implemented detection feature or measured data.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed. Present the 30–90 day window as an illustrative example threshold the owner sets, never as a Bareni benchmark, observed finding or validated rule; keep the diagnostic question as a question, and do not let it read as an invitation to a meeting."},{"claim_id":"Q03","category":"QUALIFICATIONS","evidence":[{"source_id":"C02","quote":"general document, email, CRM, and back-office
  workflows using AI plus Zapier, Make, n8n, and small amounts of custom code"},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"The diagnostic identifies the one recurring workflow, says honestly whether AI
  fits, and—if it does—defines pilot scope, fixed price, and measures."},{"source_id":"C03","quote":"Some prospecting works but depends on an
  older LinkedIn-search vendor and has encountered usage limits"}],"rationale":"Approved evidence supports CRM/email/back-office workflow automation as a service, so a contact-flagging workflow is plausibly in scope. But the claim states the boundary as settled fact ("is within scope") without the approved condition that scope and fit are decided per case in the diagnostic, and without distinguishing this from any built system; no contact-decay flag exists as a demonstrated capability.","use_guidance":"Add the qualification that this describes a workflow type Bareni can build within its stated service scope, subject to the diagnostic's honest fit assessment and the customer's existing digital tools — not an existing product or demonstrated contact-decay feature. Also avoid implying cost comparisons as measured savings; the hire-versus-automation comparison is persona framing only. Do not connect this to Atlas Partner prospecting, whose limits are disclosed."},{"claim_id":"Q04","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Turn the abstract topic into a bounded Bareni workflow decision. Explain one practical next step."},{"source_id":"C02","quote":"Normal sequence: free 30-minute diagnostic; free one-page pilot proposal;
  paid working MVP in days; fixed-price pilot in weeks"}],"rationale":"A manual next step the owner performs themselves, framed as a proposal rather than a claim about implemented software or observed results.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed as a manual owner-side audit. Per the approved CTA rule (none), do not phrase the closing as a foundation for a diagnostic conversation with Bareni or any other meeting prompt; keep it as a self-observation step."},{"claim_id":"Q05","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"C01","quote":"Especially suitable businesses already work in English, use digital
  documents and SaaS tools, and have a frequent, repeatable workflow with a
  measurable outcome."},{"source_id":"C04","quote":"Bareni currently declines high-sensitivity medical, legal, and financial work;
  bulk cold-email automation; scan-heavy OCR-dependent workflows"},{"source_id":"S01","quote":"Do not force AI where it is unsuitable."}],"rationale":"A permissible fit recommendation consistent with the approved suitability criteria and the instruction not to force AI; it asserts no current deployment or result.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed as a fit condition. Frame unsuitability as current scope discipline rather than a claim that such work can never be automated, and do not describe voice/walk-in or scan-heavy handling as a capability Bareni has."},{"claim_id":"Q06","category":"PROPOSED","evidence":[{"source_id":"S01","quote":"**CTA rule:** None."},{"source_id":"C05","quote":"Informational posts use no CTA or one soft closing sentence."}],"rationale":"A planned closing instruction that explicitly avoids a meeting invitation; it makes no factual assertion about Bareni capability or outcomes.","use_guidance":"Keep explicitly proposed. Close with a neutral observation only — no booking, call, discussion or "let's talk" phrasing, no scarcity, and no implied saving or ROI from measuring decay."}]}

